# The build context is the repo root (both images need the workspace root
# manifest + lockfile), so everything not needed to install and build is
# excluded here — it keeps the context small and, more importantly, keeps
# host-only state out of the images.

# Installed/derived state — the images install and build from scratch.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.yarn/install-state.gz
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage

# Secrets and host-specific configuration. These are supplied at *runtime* by
# docker-compose (env_file), never baked into an image: a value copied in at
# build time would also be wrong, since it describes the host's layout
# (localhost ports, on-disk sqlite path) rather than the container network's.
**/.env
**/.env.local

# The host's sqlite database. The container's lives on a mounted volume.
packages/backend/prisma/*.db
packages/backend/prisma/*.db-journal
data

# Docs, specs and design scratch — not inputs to a build.
.git
.github
.claude
openspec
design-mock
resources
*.md
docker-compose*.yml
**/*.log
.DS_Store
